IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Singapore Broadcasting Authority (Broadcasting and Television) (Amendment) Regulations 1999 (S 212/1999), made under s 79 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297), the Broadcasting Act's former name.
-- Deposit: ../../../singapore-broadcasting-authority-broadcasting-and-television-amendment-regulations-1999/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S212-1999.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited).
-- First published 14 May 1999 at 5:00 pm; made 12 May 1999; "shall come into operation on 14th May 1999". It amends regulation 8 of what became Rg 1 (the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations).
-- Only the amended words are printed, not the regulation: the full text of reg 8 as it stood after this amendment is the Revised Edition 2004's (`sgba-i-rg1.l4`), which lists S 212/99 as the last amendment before it.

§ `Paragraph 2: regulation 8 amended`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 14th May 1999 at 5:00 pm.
-- src:21 | Citation and commencement
-- src:22 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Singapore Broadcasting
-- src:23 | Authority (Broadcasting and Television) (Amendment) Regulations
-- src:24 | 1999 and shall come into operation on 14th May 1999.
-- src:26 | Amendment of regulation 8
-- src:27 | 2. Regulation 8 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority
-- src:28 | (Broadcasting and Television) Regulations (Rg 1) is amended by
-- src:29 | deleting the words ‘‘, grant an exemption from’’ and substituting the
-- src:30 | words ‘‘and subject to such conditions as it may think fit, waive or
-- src:31 | reduce’’.
@ref S 212/1999 publication line, para 1 (commencement) and para 2 (reg 8: "grant an exemption from" becomes "and subject to such conditions as it may think fit, waive or reduce") (src:3-31)
-- From 14 May 1999 the regulation reads "waive or reduce", subject to conditions, in place of "grant an exemption from" (as the old words are printed in the amendment). The encoding states only the power the amended words give.
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 212/1999 reg 8 the licensing authority's power is to waive or reduce the fee, subject to conditions, on this day` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 14 5 1999)
